# BMH course visual generation correction

For BMH course stills and animations, do not replace failed AI-generated stills with deterministic/vector/SVG/slide-icon-style plates. Jarrad explicitly rejected that look on Lesson 18B b04 quality-check and b02 county-map replacements because it does not match the existing course style and looks bad beside prior approved assets.

Future agents must stop and re-anchor to approved course visuals before generating replacements. Use the established BMH doodle still style from approved lesson assets and references, not clean vector UI diagrams, thick geometric SVG panels, or presentation-style icon boards. If a scene concept is unclear, rewrite the visual concept first and ask for approval before making more assets.

For Lesson 18B specifically, the deterministic b02/b04 replacements generated on 2026-07-07 should be treated as rejected, not as approved stills or assembly inputs.

